# Security headers for every page and file of this site (Cloudflare Pages reads this file).
# The same file is in home/, pdf/ and cad/: keep the three copies identical.
#
# Content-Security-Policy: only this site's own files run, plus Cloudflare Web Analytics
# (static.cloudflareinsights.com loads its script, cloudflareinsights.com receives the counts);
# the download buttons may ask api.github.com for the newest release; the AlternativeTo
# badge (pdf/, cad/) is a picture from alternativeto.net. Nothing may embed these
# pages in a frame, and there are no forms or plugins.
#
# Cache-Control is Cloudflare Pages' own default (always check for a newer copy) plus
# no-transform, for every address, the not-found page (404.html, served at any address)
# included: with it Cloudflare inserts no scripts. On the free plan it would add an inline
# bot-detection script ("JavaScript Detections", which can't be switched off there) that the
# policy blocks. Cloudflare Pages still adds the Web Analytics script itself, from
# static.cloudflareinsights.com, which the policy allows: don't add it by hand too.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; connect-src 'self' https://api.github.com https://cloudflareinsights.com; img-src 'self' https://alternativeto.net; style-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate, no-transform
